---
name: sprint-plan
version: 1.2.0
description: Generate a sprint plan document for repository phases. Naming is lower case - id `<phase>-<n>` (bc-4), branch `sprint/<phase>-<n>-<slug>`, target `integrate/phase-<phase>`, output `docs/plans/phase-<phase>/sprint-<phase>-<n>-<slug>.md`.
format: markdown
required_variables:
  - id
  - title
  - branch
  - target
  - closure_type
  - target_boundary
optional_variables:
  - owned_paths
  - vertical_rationale
  - lead
  - status
  - worktree
  - recommended_agent
  - recommended_model
  - dependencies_relation
  - goal
  - dependencies
  - exact_targets
  - deliverables
  - required_work
  - explicit_code_samples
  - non_closure
  - acceptance_criteria
  - validation
defaults:
  owned_paths: []
  vertical_rationale: ""
  lead: team-lead
  status: planned
  worktree: ""
  recommended_agent: ""
  recommended_model: ""
  dependencies_relation: []
  goal: []
  dependencies: []
  exact_targets: []
  deliverables: []
  required_work: []
  explicit_code_samples: []
  non_closure: []
  acceptance_criteria: []
  validation:
    - "cargo build --workspace"
    - "cargo test --workspace"
    - "cargo clippy --workspace -- -D warnings"
    - "git diff --check"
---
---
id: {{ id }}
title: {{ title }}
status: {{ status }}
branch: {{ branch }}
{% if worktree %}worktree: {{ worktree }}
{% endif %}{% if recommended_agent %}recommended_agent: {{ recommended_agent }}
{% endif %}{% if recommended_model %}recommended_model: {{ recommended_model }}
{% endif %}target: {{ target }}
closure_type: {{ closure_type }}
target_boundary: {{ target_boundary }}
---

# Sprint {{ id }} — {{ title }}

{% if recommended_agent or recommended_model %}## Recommended Agent / Model

{% if recommended_agent %}Recommended agent: {{ recommended_agent }}.
{% endif %}{% if recommended_model %}Recommended model: {{ recommended_model }}.
{% endif %}Planning advice; {{ lead }} assigns from the active pool.

{% endif %}## Goal

{% for item in goal %}- {{ item }}
{% endfor %}
## Closure

Closure type: `{{ closure_type }}` (`contract`, `boundary`, `integration` or
`docs`; see `.claude/skills/plan-hardening/sprint-planning-guidelines.md`).
Target boundary: `{{ target_boundary }}`.
{% if vertical_rationale %}
Vertical rationale (this sprint spans more than one boundary): {{ vertical_rationale }}
{% endif %}

## Owned Paths

No other sprint in the same wave may own a path matched here.

{% for path in owned_paths %}- `{{ path }}`
{% endfor %}

## Hard Dependencies

{% for dep in dependencies %}- {{ dep }}
{% endfor %}
{% if dependencies_relation %}## Dependency Relations

`must_follow` merge-forward trigger: parent development is pushed, not QA;
merge parent → child before every dev/fix round. PR-completion trigger: parent
PR merges first. `parallel_safe` is the default: no gate; state
non-intersecting ownership. A `must_follow` rationale names the contract
artifact this sprint consumes; "same file" is a split defect, not a rationale.

{% for relation in dependencies_relation %}- {{ relation.sprint }} ({{ relation.relation }} — {{ relation.rationale }})
{% endfor %}{% endif %}
## Exact Targets

{% for file in exact_targets %}- `{{ file }}`
{% endfor %}
## Deliverables

Every listed deliverable is expected to land at a production-ready level for
the closure type this sprint claims. A `boundary` sprint closes its one crate
against the fixed contract and its contract tests; behaviour that passes
through other crates is listed under "This Sprint Does Not Close" and owned
by an integration sprint. If the deliverables cannot land cleanly in one
sprint, split along boundaries into siblings that can share a wave. No
deliverable may be silently dropped or partially deferred.

{% for item in deliverables %}- {{ item }}
{% endfor %}
## Required Work

{% for item in required_work %}- {{ item }}
{% endfor %}
## Explicit Code Samples

If the sprint introduces or changes important traits, features, enums, protocol
types, boundary contracts, or execution seams, this section must include
explicit code samples or signatures showing the intended end state.

{% for item in explicit_code_samples %}{{ item }}
{% endfor %}
## This Sprint Does Not Close

Name the integration sprint that closes each item.

{% for item in non_closure %}- {{ item }}
{% endfor %}
## Acceptance Criteria

Each criterion carries its root: `boundary:<boundary_id>` in `contract` and
`boundary` sprints, `req:<ID>` in integration sprints.

{% for criterion in acceptance_criteria %}- {{ criterion }}
{% endfor %}
## Required Validation

{% for cmd in validation %}- `{{ cmd }}`
{% endfor %}
